# Rustab environment variables — reference template.
#
# Copy to `.env` if your shell or editor loads one (`.env` is gitignored).
# NOTE: Rustab itself does NOT read a `.env` file. It reads the real process
# environment, so these variables have to be exported by whatever starts the
# app:
#
#     RUSTAB_TARGET_PATH=/etc/fstab cargo tauri dev
#
# See docs/API_CONTRACT.md §2 for the full target-resolution policy.

# Which file Rustab reads and writes. Unset (the default, in both debug and
# release builds) means a per-user sandbox file is created and used:
# $XDG_DATA_HOME/rustab/fstab.sandbox, falling back to
# $HOME/.local/share/rustab/fstab.sandbox.
#
# Setting this to /etc/fstab is the ONLY way to point Rustab at the real
# system file. Doing so turns on the UI's danger banner, the extra
# confirmation checkbox before a save, and the single pkexec-elevated write
# path. Any other value is treated as an ordinary unprivileged file.
#
# For hand testing against a realistic file, point it at a private copy
# instead of the real thing (dev-data/ is gitignored — see docs/SPEC.md §7):
#RUSTAB_TARGET_PATH=dev-data/fstab.real-copy
